From: Arch POWER
Subject: [PATCH] mesa: add missing <cstddef> and <limits> includes for GCC 16

Two files use std::size_t and std::numeric_limits without including the
headers that declare them. They build where a transitive include happens
to supply the declaration; GCC 16 tightened its own headers and no longer
does, so both fail:

  src/intel/compiler/gen/gen_private.h:94: std::size_t has not been declared
  src/gallium/drivers/r600/sfn/sfn_valuefactory.cpp:746:
      numeric_limits is not a member of std

Include what each file uses. Not architecture-specific; observed on
ppc64le with GCC 16.1.1, will affect every target on that compiler.

---
--- a/src/intel/compiler/gen/gen_private.h	2026-09-06 18:27:03.882364106 -0600
+++ b/src/intel/compiler/gen/gen_private.h	2026-09-06 18:27:03.880488518 -0600
@@ -3,6 +3,8 @@
  * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
  */
 
+#include <cstddef>
+
 #include "gen.h"
 #include "gen_names.h"
 
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/r600/sfn/sfn_valuefactory.cpp	2026-09-06 18:27:03.884628843 -0600
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/r600/sfn/sfn_valuefactory.cpp	2026-09-06 18:27:03.881438288 -0600
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include "sfn_instr.h"
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <limits>
 #include <iostream>
 #include <queue>
 #include <sstream>
